{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3151","artifact_type":"feature-context","name":"plan/feature-context-sam-task-file-language.md@sha256:13780cb91925e38a8e0dc691973256c583ab5bdbdcd52933b70597e1e54a4a67"},"owner_reference":"3151","content":"# ARTIFACT:DISCOVERY\n\n## Feature\n\nRemove file-based SAM-task language from the session-context data contract and from\nrequired reading\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nA SAM task is a backend record addressed as `P{id}/T{id}`, never a file \u2014 except inside the\nlocal-YAML backend, where file storage is genuinely correct. Two authoritative, non-prose\nsources nonetheless keep teaching the file model, which is why ~6 months of prose-only\ncorrections have not closed the issue: prose is the loop's *output*, so each correction fixes\nthe open file and leaves the generators intact.\n\n**Source 1 \u2014 a live data contract.** `sam_schema/core/models.py:749` declares\n`ActiveTaskContext.task_file_path: str` as a *required* field, described as \"Absolute path to\nthe plan YAML file containing this task.\" `ActiveTaskContext` is the session-to-task binding\npersisted as `active-task-{session_id}.json` and read by the SubagentStop hook. Because the\nfield is required, the three ContextBackend implementations that have no files fabricate a\nvalue to satisfy it: `memory_context_backend.py:59` (`f\"{plan_dir}/{plan}.yaml\"`),\n`github_context_backend.py:181,350-363`, and `beads.py:1306,1378-1389` (both via a\n`_resolve_task_file_path` helper explicitly commented as mirroring the local backend). The\nconsumer then reverse-engineers the address back out of that fabricated string:\n`task_status_hook.py` reads `context_data[\"task_file_path\"]` and regexes the plan address out\nof the path (`_extract_plan_addr_from_path`). An agent or hook reading this payload is correct\nto call the thing a task file \u2014 that is what the field is named and what it holds.\n\n**Source 2 \u2014 required reading.** `AGENTS.md`'s \"Required Reading by Task Type\" routes task work\nto `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` (577 lines) at lines 115 and 409. An agent reads `AGENTS.md`, is\ntold to load the file-format doc, learns tasks are files, and writes that into whatever it\nedits \u2014 in good faith, and consistently with the live JSON key.\n\nConsequences already observed in-tree: `agents/code-reviewer.md` says \"Read the SAM task file\nusing `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_task`\" (right operation, wrong noun); `skills/execution/SKILL.md`\nhas a \"Read Task File\" workflow step; `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` documents a\n`task_file_path` parameter; `skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md` defines the `plan` field\nas \"relative path to SAM task file\". A path-based handoff also produces a silent empty read in a\nworktree-isolated dispatch rather than an error, and on a remote backend there is no file at all.\n\nA partial migration stalled here too: `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py:75-79`\nasserts `\"task_file_path\" not in source` for `sam_schema/server.py` alone, pinning one clean\nmodule while leaving the field unconstrained in every backend.\n\nScope note: the sibling problem on the SAM *plan* side (swarm-task-planner's file-authoring\nmodel, `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md`) was already closed by merged PRs #3159,\n#3161, #3137, #3156. This discovery scopes only the *task*-side fix that remains open.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. No ContextBackend other than the local-YAML one constructs, resolves, or defaults a task file\n   path to satisfy `ActiveTaskContext`.\n2. The `/dh:start-task` session-context payload identifies the active task by its plan/task\n   address, and every reader of that payload (`task_status_hook.py`,\n   `implementation_manager.py`) obtains the address directly rather than parsing it out of a\n   path string.\n3. `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` is retired and `AGENTS.md` no longer routes agents to it as\n   required reading; every document that links to it is updated as part of the retirement.\n4. Remaining agent-facing prose describing SAM tasks as files (outside the local-YAML backend's\n   own code and docs, and outside legacy-migration code) is swept, once nothing structural\n   regenerates it.\n5. The existing single-module boundary assertion in\n   `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py` is generalized to cover every non-file\n   backend, so the pattern cannot silently reappear.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n\n1. Not touching the local-YAML backend's genuinely file-based internals\n   (`local_context_backend.py`, `local_yaml.py`, `writers/yaml_writer.py`, `readers/*`, and\n   their tests) \u2014 that vocabulary is correct there.\n2. Not redoing the plan-side sweep already completed in #3159/#3161/#3137/#3156, nor\n   re-opening `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md`.\n3. Not removing file storage as a valid backend option \u2014 only removing the *shared session\n   context model's* assumption that every backend has one.\n4. Not touching legacy-format migration code/tests (`migrate_tasks_to_github.py`,\n   `test_cli_migrate_fallback.py`, `nonstandard_frontmatter_tasks.md`) \u2014 those read the old\n   format by design.\n5. Not editing `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md`. The original issue called it a\n   duplicate; it is a 7-line redirect stub to the canonical doc (consolidated 2026-03-31).\n   Verified this session. It only needs whatever the canonical doc's retirement implies for a\n   dangling redirect \u2014 nothing to delete as a duplicate.\n6. Not editing `graphify-out/*` \u2014 generated artifacts that regenerate from source.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n\n1. Every ContextBackend (local-YAML, memory, GitHub, beads) binds a session to a task by\n   address; no backend other than local-YAML exposes or synthesizes a filesystem path for that\n   binding.\n2. The `/dh:start-task` session-context JSON identifies the task by plan/task address rather\n   than by a filesystem path, and its readers consume that address as a first-class field\n   instead of deriving it from a path.\n3. `AGENTS.md`'s \"Required Reading by Task Type\" no longer presents a file-format document as\n   the authoritative task model; agents are routed to the address-based model instead.\n4. Documents that currently link to `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` do not point at a retired or\n   dangling target after the retirement.\n5. `sam_schema/core/query.py`'s module-level and function-level documentation makes clear that\n   its file/directory reasoning is local-YAML-format work, not a general statement about how\n   SAM tasks are stored. (Verified this session: this is a documentation-tone requirement, not\n   a structural one \u2014 see Resolved Questions.)\n6. Agent, skill, and documentation markdown outside the local-YAML backend's own docs and\n   legacy-migration code contains no file-based task read/write instructions after the sweep.\n\n### Non-Functional\n\n1. The live hook dispatch path must keep working: `hooks/hooks.json` wires\n   `task_status_hook.py` into `PostToolUse` (matcher `Write|Edit|Bash`) and `SubagentStop`\n   (matcher `^task-worker$`, 60s timeout). Every task-worker completion round-trips through the\n   changed field today, so this is a functional-regression risk, not a docs risk.\n2. Local-YAML backend test suites (`tests_sam/test_yaml_writer.py`, `test_detect.py`,\n   `test_yaml_reader.py`, `test_frontmatter_reader.py`, etc.) continue to pass unchanged.\n3. The four test files that exercise the field with literal path fixtures\n   (`tests/test_task_status_hook.py`, `tests_backlog/test_task_status_hook_beads.py`,\n   `tests/test_dh_paths_integration.py`,\n   `sam_schema/tests/test_parent_issue_number_widening.py`) are updated as part of this work,\n   not left asserting a fabricated path.\n4. Any code path not yet migrated must fail loudly (type error / missing required field) rather\n   than silently reading a stale or absent value.\n5. Pre-existing `active-task-{session_id}.json` files written before the change are a\n   compatibility surface the plan must consciously decide about \u2014 the model's own docstring\n   documents an additive-fields policy (\"existing files without these fields remain valid\"),\n   and this change removes or renames a required field, which is the first non-additive change\n   to that schema.\n\n## Design Questions for Planning\n\n<!-- HOW-shaped content, deliberately kept out of Requirements. -->\n\n1. **Fix ordering.** The issue author proposed structural-first: (a) rename/remove the context\n   field and delete the fabricating helpers, (b) retire `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` and its\n   `AGENTS.md` required-reading entries, (c) only then sweep prose. Evaluate whether (a) and (b)\n   can run in parallel with (c) gated behind both. Note the author's original step \"delete the\n   layer-0 duplicate\" is void \u2014 see Anti-Goal 5.\n2. **Field design.** `ActiveTaskContext` already carries additive `plan`, `task`, and `plan_dir`\n   fields described as structured addresses, so a rename target exists rather than needing a\n   from-scratch schema. Decide between: drop `task_file_path` outright and promote\n   `plan`/`task` to required; keep a path as an optional local-YAML-only field; or split the\n   model. Weigh against NFR5 (existing on-disk context files).\n3. **Consumer coupling is not cosmetic.** `implementation_manager.py:1354-1371` takes\n   `task_file_path` as a parameter, derives `plan_ref` via `plan_id_from_path()`, and\n   constructs `LocalYamlTaskProvider(task_file_path.parent)` from it; `task_status_hook.py`\n   regexes the plan address out of the path via `_extract_plan_addr_from_path`. Decide how\n   these obtain a provider and an address once no path is supplied \u2014 this is the substantive\n   engineering in the item, not the rename.\n4. **Retirement vs. rewrite of `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`.** 13 files reference it (verified this\n   session, list in References). Decide whether it is deleted with its links rewritten to the\n   address-based model, or replaced in place by an address-model document that keeps inbound\n   links valid.\n5. **Boundary-test shape.** Decide how to generalize\n   `test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py`'s source-grep assertion across backend modules\n   without also failing the legitimate local-YAML backend.\n6. **`query.py` scope.** Confirm the Impact Radius finding holds at implementation time \u2014 that\n   only the backend-agnostic `_new_plan_id()` crosses into `beads.py`/`memory.py` \u2014 and treat\n   the rest as docstring wording, unless that verification changes.\n\n## References\n\n- Issue #3151 \u2014 this item's own Root-Cause Analysis, Impact Radius, Fact-Check, RT-ICA, Issue\n  Classification, and Design Intent Alignment sections carry the full structural analysis\n- Structural sources: `sam_schema/core/models.py:749`; `AGENTS.md:115,409`\n- Fabricating backends: `memory_context_backend.py:59`;\n  `github_context_backend.py:181,350-363`; `beads.py:1306,1378-1389`\n- Genuine (excluded): `local_context_backend.py:72,128`\n- Live consumers: `task_status_hook.py:322,363,457-468,714,729`;\n  `implementation_manager.py:1354-1371`; `hooks/hooks.json` (verify, do not edit)\n- Tests exercising the field: `tests/test_task_status_hook.py`,\n  `tests_backlog/test_task_status_hook_beads.py`, `tests/test_dh_paths_integration.py`,\n  `sam_schema/tests/test_parent_issue_number_widening.py`\n- Boundary-test precedent: `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py:75-79`\n- Retirement target: `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` (577 lines). 13 files reference it (verified by\n  `grep -rl TASK_FILE_FORMAT --include=\"*.md\"` this session): `AGENTS.md`,\n  `docs/backend-providers.md`, `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`, `docs/backlog-lifecycle.md`,\n  `docs/beads-and-workflow-usage.md`, `docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md`,\n  `docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md`, `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/README.md`,\n  `docs/sdlc-layers/la